disposition gate: every merge in the window without a row is record-class -- its own diff touched only the record's own files (docs/delivery/*.md, .claude/workflows/carry-*.json, docs/plan-*.md), so it is the record being written and is self-disposing: #2454 (5b9c33d). The instrument said:
DELIVERY STATUS OK — 173 rowed, 1 pending, 0 overdue (overdue at 12 commits)
  pending  #2454 5b9c33d 0 commit(s) since — Record rows for #2445, #2453. Leaves #201 open.

This check is NOT a required context and a red here blocks no merge. Pending is the ordinary state: the protocol writes rows in batches, and only OVERDUE means a batch has stopped being drained.
--require-rows reads the same ledger under `record`'s bar rather than this lane's: a red blocks the STAMP. Every merge listed above without a row is one the tag is about to move the window's start past, and no later window can see it again.
